  "result": "I fixed it, and the full test suite passes (1908 passed).\n\n**Cause:** Shell completion splits the command line with `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. That function uses Python's `shlex.shlex`, which by default treats `#` as the start of a comment and throws away everything after it. So `cli my#file` came through as `[\"cli\", \"my\"]`, and `cli #file` lost its last argument entirely, which led to wrong completions. Python's `shlex.split` turns comment handling off, but this code builds the lexer directly and never did.\n\n**Fix:** One line added after `lex.whitespace_split = True`:\n\n```python\nlex.commenters = \"\"\n```\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_parser.py`: `cli my#file` and `cli #file`. Both fail without the fix and pass with it.\n\nThe changes aren't committed.",
